<Layout title="Pay Small Small at Hubtel — David Glover" description="Building the Flutter mobile implementation of Pay Small Small at Hubtel: account experiences, repayments, transaction history, and connected financial journeys.">
<section class="case-hero"><a class="back-link" href="/#work">← Back to selected work</a><p class="eyebrow">HUBTEL / PROFESSIONAL WORK</p><h1>Everyday credit.<br /><span class="blue">Thoughtfully connected.</span></h1><p class="case-lead">Building the mobile implementation of Pay Small Small—and connecting the details that make a financial experience feel coherent.</p><dl class="case-facts"><div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Mobile Product Engineer</dd></div><div><dt>Platform</dt><dd>Hubtel consumer app</dd></div><div><dt>Technology</dt><dd>Flutter · Dart</dd></div><div><dt>Status</dt><dd>In production</dd></div></dl></section>
<div class="case-banner hubtel-cover"><div><img class="case-brand hubtel-brand" src="/images/brands/hubtel.png" alt="Hubtel" width="303" height="192" /><h2>Purchase. Repay.<br />Keep track.</h2></div><p>One connected mobile experience for Pay Small Small.</p></div>
<div class="case-content"><section class="case-section"><p class="eyebrow">THE CONTEXT</p><h2>Credit is a journey, not a screen.</h2><p>Pay Small Small lets Hubtel customers make eligible purchases and repay in smaller amounts. For customers, that means more than choosing a payment method: they need to understand their account, see what’s coming up, and know what to do next.</p><p>I built the feature’s mobile implementation in Flutter, connecting the services behind Pay Small Small to the customer experience within Hubtel’s existing app.</p><div class="case-actions"><a class="text-link" href="https://hubtel.com/pay-small-small">About Pay Small Small at Hubtel <Icon name="external" /></a></div></section>
<section class="case-section"><p class="eyebrow">MY CONTRIBUTION</p><h2>The connected mobile experience.</h2><p>My ownership covered the Pay Small Small mobile feature, including its account overview, upcoming paybacks, statements, and repayment journeys. This was mobile implementation within the wider Hubtel product and its supporting services.</p><ul><li><strong>Account visibility:</strong> bringing account information and upcoming repayments into the same experience.</li><li><strong>Transaction history:</strong> paginated statements, grouped by date, so customers can explore their history.</li><li><strong>Repayment journeys:</strong> connecting repayment requests, payment approval, and a top-up path when additional funds are needed.</li><li><strong>Account continuity:</strong> refreshing information as customers return from deposits, make repayments, or revisit their account.</li></ul></section>
<section class="case-section"><p class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING FOCUS</p><h2>Making the return journey matter.</h2><p>A customer can move between their account, a repayment, and a deposit. Those screens need to reconnect when the customer returns, with the relevant account information refreshed.</p><p>The implementation coordinates shared account state with the Pay Small Small view model. It loads related account information together, refreshes on return paths, and retrieves statement history in pages.</p><div class="case-callout"><p>The important detail is what happens between screens: a financial journey should remain understandable as the customer moves through it.</p></div></section>
<section class="case-section"><p class="eyebrow">BEYOND PAY SMALL SMALL</p><h2>The account experience around it.</h2><p>My work at Hubtel also includes login and authentication, along with account features such as notifications, payment history, verification and PIN, refunds and rewards, and app appearance.</p><p>These are the everyday touchpoints that surround the main payment experience. They give my work a broader focus on how people access, understand, and manage their accounts.</p></section>
